    "title": "pandas.Timestamp.tzinfo — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1386.gcb2086a1a4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Timestamp.tzinfo#\n\n- property Timestamp.tzinfo#\n- Returns the timezone info of the Timestamp. This property returns a datetime.tzinfo object if the Timestamp is timezone-aware. If the Timestamp has no timezone, it returns None. If the Timestamp is in UTC or a fixed-offset timezone, it returns datetime.timezone. If the Timestamp uses an IANA timezone (e.g., “America/New_York”), it returns zoneinfo.ZoneInfo. See also \n  - `Timestamp.tz`\n  - Alias for tzinfo, may return a zoneinfo.ZoneInfo object.\n  - `Timestamp.tz_convert`\n  - Convert timezone-aware Timestamp to another time zone.\n  - `Timestamp.tz_localize`\n  - Localize the Timestamp to a specific timezone.\n Examples >>> ts = pd.Timestamp(\"2023-01-01 12:00:00\", tz=\"UTC\") >>> ts.tzinfo datetime.timezone.utc >>> ts_naive = pd.Timestamp(\"2023-01-01 12:00:00\") >>> ts_naive.tzinfo",
